---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy and cookies"
  description="What DataTales records about visits, and how to change your cookie choice."
>
  <div class="container measure">
    <h1>Privacy and cookies</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        DataTales has no accounts, comments or sign-up forms, so it does not ask for your name or
        email address.
      </p>

      <h2>Google Analytics (only if you accept)</h2>
      <p>
        With your permission, the site uses Google Analytics to count visits and see which stories
        are read. If you accept, your browser loads Google's analytics script, and Google sets
        cookies whose names start with <code>_ga</code> to tell repeat visits apart. Google then
        receives details such as the pages you view, your browser and device type, and your
        approximate location. Google Analytics is provided by Google; see{' '}
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's privacy policy</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you reject, or make no choice, the analytics script is never loaded and no analytics
        cookie is set.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choice</h2>
      <p>
        You can change your mind at any time with <strong>Cookie settings</strong> at the bottom of
        every page. Choosing Reject removes the analytics cookies from this site.
      </p>

      <h2>Other things the site stores</h2>
      <p>
        Your browser's local storage keeps your light/dark theme and your cookie choice. These stay
        on your device and are not sent anywhere.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        This site is run by {SITE.author}. See the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
